<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Germany</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger</id><updated>2026-11-06T21:39:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-ger" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-ger" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ilse Aigner tipped by party allies as next German president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ce0535a581ba0ce86aabddb1136f5ba2609021f402f49f3caf4008be0a5c717</id><updated>2026-11-06T21:39:28Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T18:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ilse-aigner-tipped-by-party-allies-as-next-german-president/a-79880594--62497e57d523.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ilse-aigner-tipped-by-party-allies-as-next-german-president/a-79880594?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German media reports suggest that Bavarian politician Ilse Aigner's chances of becoming the next president are on the up. Long favored by her Bavarian CSU, now it seems Christian Democrats nationwide plan to back her.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Small plane crashes onto A2 highway, killing 2</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0b22df14d1aefb099a25002e68f76c377847b87359234ce48b273bd6a1f0963</id><updated>2026-11-06T21:39:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-06T16:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-small-plane-crashes-onto-a2-highway-killing-2/a-79878930--fda2d6a1e11f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-small-plane-crashes-onto-a2-highway-killing-2/a-79878930?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two people have died after a small plane crashed onto Germany's A2 highway near Magdeburg. The crash closed the Hannover-bound lanes on a major east-west route, with no road vehicles reported to be involved.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Deportations on the decline</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d86dd6d9ba0c50d1b40027f807eefafba04dbd8f6d7381a28c52a57dc45777d</id><updated>2026-11-06T21:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T09:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-deportations-on-the-decline/live-79860126--231ad2fcde65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-deportations-on-the-decline/live-79860126?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite a decrease in overall deportations, more people were sent back to Turkey. Meanwhile, Volkswagen is facing a fresh "Dieselgate" trial. And Germany's leading DAX stock index hit a new high. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bavarian politician Hubert Aiwanger found dead in Berlin hotel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce3c919809177a25b435cb4f9c0131502c47858ecb9a36f513904038d9fd5d38</id><updated>2026-11-06T21:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bavarian-politician-hubert-aiwanger-found-dead-in-berlin-hotel/a-79859115--a5e0e6ba38b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bavarian-politician-hubert-aiwanger-found-dead-in-berlin-hotel/a-79859115?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Aiwanger was Bavaria's Economy Minister and the chairman of the right-wing populist Free Voters party. The circumstances surrounding his death are still unclear.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s Gen Z protests spark debate on integration, bias</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2b64639f327faa82a7d3a134ea3a01abf59b89f3177c7f3e9ce87297173c3d6</id><updated>2026-11-06T21:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T16:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-spark-debate-on-integration-bias/a-79868497--c2e5ae27f840.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-spark-debate-on-integration-bias/a-79868497?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Political debate about the recent Gen Z riots have raised the question: Can Germany talk about problems with integration without putting entire groups of people under suspicion?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Pioneering Jewish academy opens in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65e9f30b18582d4e6b35821b88bf125fdecf75122ece581cb3716dff10073b6b</id><updated>2026-11-06T21:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T11:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pioneering-jewish-academy-opens-in-germany/a-79863293--10bb65c14f4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pioneering-jewish-academy-opens-in-germany/a-79863293?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Jewish academy has opened its doors in Frankfurt. The Central Council of Jews in Germany, the country’s leading Jewish umbrella group, set up the project to combat hate and promote dialogue and learning nationally.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>The 2011 discovery of neo-Nazi killers aired biases in German policing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:185f98344238dfde3289af4e6037dfe2891eb4db881ac7bdca1be3bf791d2040</id><updated>2026-11-06T21:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-2011-discovery-of-neo-nazi-killers-aired-biases-in-german-policing/a-79857781--949d4ea66003.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-2011-discovery-of-neo-nazi-killers-aired-biases-in-german-policing/a-79857781?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Many questions still surround the National Socialist Underground whose existence was revealed by neo-Nazi terrorist Beate Zschäpe on November 4, 2011. How has German society reacted to NSU crimes? Has justice been done?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's celebrated children's author Janosch has died</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57263e6c49cb4edfe302c1ef01f5ea38d1dd764b6cc6808449dbd3d66eb90812</id><updated>2026-11-06T21:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600--a3fdc8a2501b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-celebrated-children-s-author-janosch-has-died/a-79851600?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bear, Tiger and Tiger-Duck: The author and illustrator Janosch achieved world fame with his heartwarming children's figures. He died at the age of 95.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>The dachshund, a humorous icon with political symbolism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcad094f4a9f7f57f486e175adf4a7fddc27e16b2628019f32c6322923422652</id><updated>2026-11-06T21:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T07:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191--0ec0144d606e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dachshund-a-humorous-icon-with-political-symbolism/a-79640191?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From Picasso to Andy Warhol, a surprising number of artists have portrayed the German breed. But the dachshund has also at times been co-opted as a political symbol.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Wagner brothers begin new NBA chapter on different paths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c1c4a17104858ee9be801111eec1c5da027abd9daf4fc2dfb72f9d6edb16e75a</id><updated>2026-11-06T21:38:22Z</updated><published>2026-10-20T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668--ff5544415c4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wagner-brothers-begin-new-nba-chapter-on-different-paths/a-79712668?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After five years, brothers Franz and Moritz Wagner are no longer playing together for the Orlando Magic. In the new NBA season, their separation will likely mean the new "German" team is the Charlotte Hornets.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
